## Submodule entries

23 rows above are `git submodule` entries, pinned by the commit SHA recorded in
the tree and mapped to their upstream URL in `.gitmodules`. Materialise them with
`git submodule update --init --recursive`, and verify with
`./scripts/check-vendor.sh`.

`pin` is `TBD` in the table because the authoritative pin is the gitlink SHA in
the tree, not a value maintained by hand here. To read a pin:

```bash
git ls-tree HEAD old/ | awk '$1=="160000"{print $4, $3}'
```

