## Licence corrections

| id | was | is | why |
|---|---|---|---|
| `srep` | `Public-Domain` / `copy-src` | `all-rights-reserved` / `reference` | The source header in `old/srep-main/Compression/SREP/srep.cpp` reads "Copyright (C) 2009-2014 Bulat Ziganshin. **All rights reserved.** Mail Bulat.Ziganshin@gmail.com ... if you want to buy a commercial license for the source code." There is no LICENSE or COPYING file in the tree. The same notice appears on the copy embedded in `old/freearc-main/clibs/Compression/SREP/srep.cpp`. |

This is the only wrong row found in a spot-check of the sources ziptastic is
likely to use. Checked and confirmed correct: `7z` PPMd (`Ppmd7.c`: "Igor Pavlov :
Public domain"), `preflate` (Apache-2.0), `brotli` (MIT), `zstd` (BSD-3),
`lz4` (BSD-2), `libbsc` (Apache-2.0). Note that `zpaq` is public domain but
bundles libdivsufsort (MIT) inside `libzpaq.cpp`, so its row is "PD + MIT".

**Consequence for consumers:** SREP is a design reference only. Its block-hash
long-range matching is a published technique and can be implemented
independently, but the code itself may not be copied into a closed-source
binary, and `copy-src` was wrong.
